      "rev_n_1_8cc483_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_8cc483_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_8cc483",
        "thought_text": "Revised Thought-1: The issue lies in the transition logic for the SPEND_SPORTS state. Specifically, the condition `if day_activity == 2 or day_activity == 3:` should also consider the possibility of transitioning from the REST state to SPEND_SPORTS when the gym is open. Additionally, the initial state setup and transitions need to ensure that Vasya does not perform the same activity on consecutive days.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_8cc483_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_f8c9413041",
        "created_at": 1794506343.771225
      },
      "rev_n_2_07d83d_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_07d83d_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_07d83d",
        "thought_text": "Dynamic Programming with State Transition\n\nConsider using dynamic programming to keep track of the minimum number of rest days while ensuring Vasya adheres to the constraints of not doing the same activity on consecutive days. Define `dp[i][j]` as the minimum number of rest days up to day `i` when Vasya performs activity `j` on day `i`. Transition between states based on the allowed activities and update the DP table accordingly. Finally, select the state with the minimum rest days for the last day.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_07d83d_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_4eca6e4481",
        "created_at": 1794506374.0975635
      },
